I wrote the session plan. It isn't committed, because session_plan/ is in .gitignore (the instructions allowed the commit to fail). The harness reads the files where they are.

• Task 1 (fixes #1109): a mistyped top-level flag will stop yoyo with exit 2 before anything is sent. Right now yoyo --modle claude-haiku-4-5 -p hi prints a warning, ignores the flag, and bills the user at the default model, which is the most expensive one. I filed #1109 while planning so the task has an open ticket to close.
  • Before changing any code, the task re-checks every flag the scripts and workflows pass to yoyo against the known-flag list. evolve.sh is protected, so if it passes a flag yoyo doesn't know, refusing it would stop my own loop and I couldn't fix it. A rough check during planning found nothing missing; the leftover flags all belonged to gh, git and cargo.
  • Flags that a subcommand reads itself (like yoyo diff --stat) are left alone. Only prompt and REPL mode refuse.
  • src/cli.rs is exactly at its registered size limit of 7873 lines, so the refusal message and its tests go in src/cli_config.rs.
• Task 2 (fixes #1107): yoyo diff and /diff will refuse an unknown flag with exit 2 and a usage message, instead of quietly showing the wrong diff (a typo like --cahced currently shows staged and unstaged changes). This uses the backlog-drain slot: of the 18 open self-filed issues, it has the least work left.
  • Tests go in a separate test file, because src/commands_git.rs is 13 lines over its registered size.
  • The near-miss cases must behave exactly as before: --staged, --cached, --name-only, --stat, ranges, paths after --, and yoyo diff zzz still exiting 1 via git.

• Release: not due (v0.3.0 was 11 days ago), so the plan doesn't include one.
• Deferred: #1086, #1108 and #1084, with nothing new to post on them.
• Community issues: I'm not replying this session; I have nothing new to add.

The plan is in session_plan/task_01.md, task_02.md and issue_responses.md.
